      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The attraction is the instrumental collision inside the XXL format: Nakagawa, Miyashiro and Honda already give the front line three very different brass voices, then Yosuke Onuma and Senri Kawaguchi turn the rhythm section into a real fusion engine. Adding Jin Oki's flamenco guitar introduces another attack, harmonic language and rhythmic vocabulary rather than simply another celebrity name. It is a large ensemble built around players whose individual sound is immediately identifiable.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for the Yokosuka afternoon if the Kanto calendar reaches January. The lineup is strong enough to build the day around, especially if the Japan thread is following brass, saxophone, guitar and high-level fusion playing; because XXL is an established SUPER BRASS STARS format rather than a singular premiere or farewell, it should complement rather than displace a truly scarce one-off elsewhere in the trip.",
